.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-override-request 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-override\-request \- Answer a class\*(Aqs declared precondition and receive an admission for one situation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten override request\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-rule\fR> <\fB\-\-verdict\fR> <\fB\-\-subject\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Answer a class\*(Aqs declared precondition and receive an admission for one situation
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\fR
The rule whose refusal is being overridden
.TP
\fB\-\-verdict\fR
The verdict token that refusal carries, e.g. diff ship early
.TP
\fB\-\-subject\fR
The gate\*(Aqs canonical subject, exactly as its refusal names it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
